# Normalise line endings on commit so a Windows checkout and a Linux CI
# produce identical blobs. This repo is source-only (no build products).
* text=auto eol=lf

# F1/t49 — the ONE exception, and why it is an exception.
#
# `domains/user-feedback/fixtures/_generate.mjs` renders these fixtures with
# CRLF (`\n` -> `\r\n`, deliberately), and
# `domains/user-feedback/test.mjs` asserts that the generator reproduces every
# committed fixture BYTE for byte (`_generate-util.mjs:compareRendered` reads the
# file and compares strings). `text=auto eol=lf` rewrites them to LF inside the
# blob, so a tree checked out of git no longer matches the generator and that
# assertion fails — while the working tree, where the generator last wrote,
# still passes. That is an inconsistency between HEAD and the working tree, i.e.
# exactly what F1 is about: `git archive HEAD | tar -x; npm test` must be green.
#
# `-text` keeps the blob byte-identical to the generator's output, which is the
# property the test asserts, and it keeps the repo's goal intact (the bytes are
# the same on Windows and on Linux — no conversion happens at all).
#
# If the generator is ever changed to emit LF, DELETE this exception with it:
# the rule is "the generator owns the bytes", not "fixtures are CRLF".
domains/user-feedback/fixtures/*.json -text

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.tgz binary
